+## Clock authority model
+
+One observation contains source ID, boot ID, calling-thread time-namespace ID,
+realtime nanoseconds, boot-relative nanoseconds, uncertainty, and synchronization
+quality. The state machine accepts only synchronized observations within durable
+uncertainty policy.
+
+Healthy state retains the first accepted/recovery observation as a drift anchor
+and the latest accepted observation. Quarantine retains the previous accepted
+evidence when available, the exact rejected observation, anomaly, high water,
+and generations. Ordinary observation cannot clear quarantine.
+
+Schema v5 stores a bounded canonical encoding of this complete state plus an
+identity-bound SHA-256 structural digest. Decode, canonical re-encode, digest
+recompute, policy revalidation, exact prior-row compare, and complete staged
+restore all occur before publication.
+
+## SQLite cutpoint
+
+Every public write operation:
+
+1. opens a typed immediate transaction;
+2. verifies writer authority;
+3. restores exact schema, durable operations, parent edges, local counter map,
+   projections, outbox, lease/retry fields, clock state, policies, and digests;
+4. applies the pure transition;
+5. writes exact prior-state-conditional changes;
+6. independently restores the complete staged cutpoint; and
+7. commits only when the observed state equals the intended state.
+
+Clock quarantine is itself a durable publication. When an anomalous observation
+is detected, the owner re-attests and commits quarantine before reporting the
+user operation failure. Restart cannot erase the anomaly merely because the
+claim, settlement, renewal, or release did not succeed.
+
+This owner is intentionally **O(history)**. It is a correctness oracle,
+migration verifier, crash scaffold, and future repair authority, not a production
+throughput claim.
 
